(To integrate multiple peripherals \(DS18B20 Temperature Sensor, OLED Display, RFID Scanner\) with an) Tj
T* (ESP32 and host a local web server to display the aggregated sensor data over WiFi.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 632.1262204724408775 Td
(Introduction:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 615.1183464566928478 Td
(Real-world IoT devices require the integration of various sensors using different communication protocols) Tj
T* (\(I2C for OLED, SPI for RFID, OneWire for DS18B20\). This lab demonstrates how to manage these buses) Tj
T* (simultaneously while also handling network requests via the ESP32's built-in WiFi capabilities.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 549.9214960629921052 Td
(1. Theoretical Concepts) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 532.9136220472440755 Td
(Bus Sharing & Protocols: The ESP32 is capable of managing multiple protocols simultaneously. The OLED) Tj
T* (uses the I2C bus \(SDA/SCL\). The DS18B20 uses the OneWire protocol which allows multiple sensors on a) Tj
T* (single data line. The MFRC522 RFID reader uses the faster SPI bus, which requires a dedicated Slave) Tj
T* (Select \(SS\) pin to coordinate data flow.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Asynchronous Web Serving: The ESP32 WebServer library listens for incoming HTTP GET requests on port) Tj
T* (80. When a client connects, the ESP32 dynamically generates an HTML string containing the latest sensor) Tj
T* (readings and serves it back to the browser.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0. g
56.6929133858267775 396.850629921259781 Td
(2. Source Code - ESP32 Server Integration) Tj
ET
